# dsh-ml-planner — line-ending discipline
#
# 1) Repo-authored files (README, docs/, scripts/, CHANGELOG …) are normalized to
#    LF in the index and checked out as LF, so a Windows checkout cannot pollute
#    the repository with CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# 2) preset/ ships the preset BYTES VERBATIM. Those bytes are hash-verified by
#    preset/scripts/verify_integrity.py against the manifest at
#    preset/skills/ml-modeling-plan/references/preset-integrity-manifest.md, so
#    git must never rewrite line endings there. Five of the shipped preset files
#    are CRLF upstream; `-text` keeps all of them byte-identical.
preset/** -text

# 3) Binary assets (docs screenshots and similar) must never be diffed or
#    line-ending-converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
